{"title":"2017 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 11","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Diagram_for_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Diagram for Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The region consisting of all points in three-dimensional space within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units of line segment <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/0/840e2b592390eb6ec918fa6f3292716ce170de66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AB}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> has volume <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/9/f099af0894a766e83c9a8af00567a186ddfa3886.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216\\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />. What is the length <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/4/9/e498a0d7159579955adab10c9bb4d3ac3178ccc0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textit{AB}$\" width=\"25\" height=\"12\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/3/6e3de5a494bb888a56d3378211e1a3d3df958aa3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6\\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 12\\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 18\\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20\\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In order to solve this problem, we must first visualize what the region looks like. We know that, in a three dimensional space, the region consisting of all points within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units of a point would be a sphere with radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.  However, we need to find the region containing all points within <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> units of a segment.  It can be seen that our region is a cylinder with two hemispheres/endcaps on either end.  We know the volume of our region, so we set up the following equation (the volume of our cylinder + the volume of our two hemispheres will equal <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6e9b84e67186f910a8832ac4e267ce1357198e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />):\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/0/b1061db52cd865c8e7abc7c1bc24215edc8a59e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4 \\pi }{3} \\cdot 3^3+9 \\pi x=216 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"168\" height=\"37\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is equal to the length of our line segment.\n</p><p>Solving, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/7/8/f786bc655d428a33a947dc31c2199a68bdecef50.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = \\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"99\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Because this is just a cylinder and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hemispheres (\"half spheres\"), and the radius is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, the volume of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hemispheres is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/b/e3b125cd191b8590da58de3e7f4e260ee4bf35d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4(3^3)\\pi}{3} = 36 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"107\" height=\"39\" />. Since we also know that the volume of this whole thing is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/6/5f6e9b84e67186f910a8832ac4e267ce1357198e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" />, we do <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/5/bf54ab41e1bbcf9d4c16b63be0cb6a86b427f6cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$216 \\pi-36 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"92\" height=\"15\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9683610d5ffafa4c0edeb89972aef25f02cb1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" /> as the volume of the cylinder. Thus the height is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/d/9/4d9683610d5ffafa4c0edeb89972aef25f02cb1a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$180 \\pi$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"37\" height=\"13\" /> divided by the area of the base, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/9/1/e917ce8beb9c5f920fa0607c1516212cc73651b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{180 \\pi}{9\\pi}=20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />, so our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/3/3e32b4b921717482e7a5d49e7f17c3887c2f8b3b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 20}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"68\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~Minor edit by virjoy2001 and slamgirls\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Diagram_for_Solution\">Diagram for Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Diagram for Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"http://i.imgur.com/cwNt293.png\">http://i.imgur.com/cwNt293.png</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/s4vnGlwwHHw\">https://youtu.be/s4vnGlwwHHw</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_11&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A\">2017 AMC 10A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Problems\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_AMC_10A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2017 AMC 10A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\